' Authored by: Emmanuel A. Otchere (cardinal author rule, 2026-09-23)
'
' Agentic Operations relational diagram
'
' Per CR-ES-007 §20 + ADR-ES-007 §26 + §30.
' Illustrates the 9 canonical relationships (specializes ;; engages ;;;
' responds-to ;; operates-within ;; governed-by ;; coordinates ;;
' uses ;; produces ;; adapts-to) plus the specialisation parent.

@startuml agentic-operations

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 10

skinparam rectangle {
    BackgroundColor #F0F8FF
    BorderColor #4682B4
}

title Agentic Operations ;;; Relational Model

' Core Agentic Operations class

rectangle "Agentic Operations\n(ES:CONCEPT:agentic-operations)" as aop #FFE4B5

' Specialization parent

rectangle "Operations\n(ES:CONCEPT:operations)" as ops #F0FFF0

' Agent engagement

rectangle "Agent\n(ES:CONCEPT:agent)" as agent #F0E8FF

' Operational context

rectangle "Operational Context\n(external:concept:operational-context)" as oc #FFFACD

' Inherited semantics

rectangle "Authority\n(ES:CONCEPT:authority)" as auth #E0FFFF
rectangle "Policy\n(external:concept:policy)" as policy #FFE4E1

' Coordinated entities

rectangle "Process\n(external:concept:process)" as process #FFFACD
rectangle "Agentic Workflow\n(ES:CONCEPT:agentic-workflow)" as awf #FFE4B5
rectangle "Operational Outcome\n(external:concept:operational-outcome)" as outcome #E0FFE0

' Relationships

aop --|> ops : specializes

aop --> agent : engages

aop --> oc : responds-to
aop --> oc : adapts-to

aop --> auth : operates-within
aop --> policy : governed-by

aop --> process : coordinates
aop --> awf : uses

aop --> outcome : produces

note bottom of aop
  Per CR-ES-007 §6 + ADR-ES-007 §2 + §21 + §30.
  Agentic Operations specialises Operations ;;
  preserves Operations semantics ;;
  adds 8 characteristics ;; 10 properties ;;
  9 canonical relationships.
end note

note right of aop
  Per ADR-ES-007 §6.7 + §6.8 + §17 ;;
  Agentic Operations operates within
  Authority and Policy ;; bounded adaptive
  operating mode.
end note

note bottom of ops
  Per CR-ES-007 §5 + ADR-ES-007 §5 ;;
  Operations is established by
  FND-ES-AG-004 ;;; ES-canonical
  established at v1.0.0.
end note

@enduml